  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I did not run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so I haven't seen a rendered frame and the camera, shadows and bird poses are untested.\n\n- **Bird:** a body, a head with a cone beak and two eyes, and a tail fan of 5 feathers. Each wing has an inner and an outer segment joined by a wrist joint. The bird is built only from primitives, with no external models.\n- **Flight:** a circle of radius 6 at constant height 3.2. One lap takes 8 seconds. The bird yaws to face its direction of travel and rolls about 0.38 rad into the turn.\n- **Flapping:** 2 flaps per second, so a lap is exactly 16 flaps and the loop closes with no jump. The outer wing lags the inner by about 0.9 rad of flap phase, so the wing bends. The body bobs by about 0.09 units with each flap.\n- **Scene:** a ground disc with a lighter meadow disc, 13 cone trees, and 2 rocks. The sky-colored background has one shadow-casting directional light and a neutral environment for fill.\n- **Camera:** it trails the bird at radius 11.5 and height 5.2, outside the flight circle. It is set to look at the bird every frame through `app.camera.setPose`.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true after `app.ready()` and one animation frame.\n\nThe flap and loop timing advances by the frame time (capped at 0.1 s per frame), so it follows frame time instead of a free-running clock.\n\n",
